From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 03:52:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] backends: tell the shell when the pointer is shaken, and draw
 it larger

The cursor tracker watches pointer motion while something listens to its
new pointer-shaken signal. It counts quick, straight strokes that turn
back on themselves, and emits at each turn once three of them land
within 600 ms, so slow drawing, swipes, circles and tremors don't count.
It sits out while a button is held, the shell holds a grab, a window is
dragged, a client locks or confines the pointer, or the pointer is
hidden.

meta_cursor_tracker_set_magnification() draws the pointer larger. Theme
cursors load at the larger size so they are only ever scaled down, the
hardware cursor plane carries them while they fit, and the cursor
overlay takes over when they don't.

Upstream-Status: luft-only Kestrel's shake to find the pointer
